<title>UK: B.A.T hit by Kleinwort downgrade.</title>
<headline>B.A.T hit by Kleinwort downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in tobacco and financial services conglomerate B.A.T Industries Plc weakened in Monday morning trade, hit by a downgrade on the stock by Kleinwort Benson Securities, market sources said.</p>
<p>B.A.T shares dropped six pence or 1.3 percent to 456-1/2p by 1017 GMT when the overall market was down almost one percent. Some 760,000 shares had changed hands.</p>
<p>Market sources said Kleinwort cut B.A.T to &quot;underweight&quot; from &quot;hold&quot; previously. They gave no further details.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
